%% HANDWRITTEN. Checked against ARCHITECTURE.md S5 + D6 + services/context/assembler.py
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C as Customer
    participant APP as Krungsri app
    participant API as ReadyCall API
    participant ID as IdentityResolver
    participant CTX as ContextAssembler
    participant CORE as Bank core (READ-ONLY)
    participant BR as BriefBuilder

    Note over C,BR: D6 - context assembly starts at TAP, not at ANSWER

    C->>APP: taps Contact on Health Plan A
    APP->>API: POST /v1/calls/intents (session cookie)
    Note right of API: identity comes from the SESSION,<br/>never from the request body (D4)
    API->>API: mint correlation token, store only its SHA-256 hash
    API-->>APP: token + the number to dial

    par context prefetch starts immediately
        API->>CTX: build(customer_id, product_code)
        CTX->>CORE: get_customer
        CTX->>CORE: list_policies
        CTX->>CORE: list_interactions
        CTX->>CORE: list_holdings
        CTX->>CORE: list_life_events
        CTX->>CORE: get_product
        Note right of CTX: 6 reads in PARALLEL (asyncio.gather)<br/>one round trip, not six
        CORE-->>CTX: rows
        CTX->>CTX: pick the relevant policy, stamp provenance per field
        CTX-->>API: frozen ContextSnapshot
    and the customer is still lifting the phone to their ear
        APP->>C: dialling...
    end

    APP->>API: the call arrives, carrying the token
    API->>ID: resolve(correlation_token)
    ID->>ID: hash it, look it up, check it has not expired
    ID-->>API: L3_VERIFIED + customer_id
    API->>BR: build_context_only(snapshot, identity)
    BR-->>API: CaseBrief v1

    Note over API,BR: the brief exists BEFORE the phone has finished ringing
